// Title: Query Usage To Exfil Data
// Sigma ID: 53ef0cef-fa24-4f25-a34a-6c72dfa2e6e2
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-08-01 | Modified: 2023-01-19
// ATT&CK: execution
// Description: Detects usage of "query.exe" a system binary to exfil information such as "sessions" and
//   "processes" for later use
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://twitter.com/MichalKoczwara/status/1553634816016498688
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_query_session_exfil.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath endswith ":\\Windows\\System32\\query.exe" and (ProcessCommandLine contains "session >" or ProcessCommandLine contains "process >")
